-- title:
--   Equal transported extra levels force e_γ-stability over the residue field
-- statement:
--   The statement is placed in the full Čerednik–Drinfeld frame, whose data and hypotheses are grouped and summarised below; the conclusion is stated in full.
--
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a non-zero squarefree natural number $N$ divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, together with an irreducible element $\pi$, the hypotheses that $\mathcal{O}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, that $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and that $(r) = (\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Next, a characteristic-zero domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, subject to the clauses `hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`, `hOnr_alg`, `hOnr_closed`, `hFr`: $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathrm{Onr}$ has a root modulo it, and $F_r(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. Finally a homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternionic moduli frame.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and its completion at a finite place $v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$, with `hΛℤ` asserting that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and an order coordinate system $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r)^{2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $q$-adic density and the trace identity). A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with moduli points $\mathrm{pt}$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and coprime to $N$, a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with points $\mathrm{ptF}$ which is a fine moduli space for full level-$n$ structures (`IsFineModuli`), and a group $G$ acting on $M$ through $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ realising level twists (`IsLevelTwistAction`). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with moduli points (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$ for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure, with degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1 : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ realising respectively forgetting the extra level and passing to an $\ell$-isogeny quotient. Endomorphisms $\mathrm{ar}, \mathrm{arbar}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on moduli points.
--
--   **Definite quaternionic side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it; an adelic unit $n_1$ in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_1\,r$ such that $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ containing $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of units is characterised by `hΓt` as $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_1\,v$, the units integral at all places other than $v$. For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $\mathrm{sf}_\ell$ satisfying `hs` (prescribed local components away from and above $r$, a Hecke condition on $\ell\cdot \mathrm{sf}_\ell^{-1}$ taken in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}$ or $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}$ according to whether $\ell \mid N$, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$), with $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w) = \bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **Data over the residue field $k_0 = \mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $k_0$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over $k_0$, two-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0$, maps $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ with $e\gamma$ over the structure morphism and degrees $\deg\gamma$, with `hA₀` asserting that the formal group of $A_0$ is $X_0$ through $\mathrm{coord}$. The clauses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'` make $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ an action up to powers of $r$: each $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving level, composition holds after multiplication by suitable powers of $r$, rational integral scalars act by multiplication, and conversely $e\gamma$ being a multiplication forces $\gamma$ to be a scalar. The clause `hE2` normalises these endomorphisms on formal coordinates: for every injective embedding of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with each $e\gamma$ induced by a centraliser element whose matrix is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$. The clause `hE3` provides, for each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$, labels $\mathrm{lab} : \Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ describing the action of $e\gamma$ on the structure, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; `hE4` asserts that over any algebraically closed extension every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny pair on a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$. A further order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators clearing $R_1$ into $R_2$, endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$, and the clauses `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e` making $\hat e$ an action of $R_2$ by level-preserving endomorphisms commuting with $\Lambda$, multiplicative, with integers acting by multiplication, with $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ the reduced norm, compatible with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$, and simultaneously matrix-normalised together with $e$.
--
--   **Drinfeld moduli side.** A ring map $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r) \to \mathrm{Onr}$, a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, and a map $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $\mathrm{MD}$ satisfying `hη` (three clauses: admissible rigidified objects have equal images exactly when isomorphic, compatibility with base change, and local surjectivity on a Zariski cover). An injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ with `hE₀` giving a fixed power $r^{m}$ bounding integrality in both directions. A system $\mathrm{eD}$ of maps from the functor $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal{O}\,\mathrm{MD}$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $\mathrm{Onr}$ with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$, together with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity on every $\pi$-nilpotent noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra), `hfstD` (the first component is the coefficient leg), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on moduli points corresponds to $\mathrm{OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct}$, that is, a Frobenius twist of the leg by $-\mathrm{vdet}$ together with pullback of the Deligne datum), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` (the $\pi$-translation twists the leg by $F_r$ and leaves the Deligne datum unchanged, and always exists). A ring map $\kappa$ from $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ to $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the special fibre: a curve $A_{0w}$, maps $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ with exponent $k_w$, the clauses `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (a joint matrix normalisation of the $e\gamma$ and of $a_w \text{ followed by } b_w$, the latter with matrix $r^{k_w'} g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$).
--
--   **Comparison maps.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with coefficient leg $\psi$ to a point of $\mathrm{MD}$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullback of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of curves compatible with the rigidification data up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description: there are $j \leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with prescribed formal module, related to the rigidification by $\mathrm{IsRigTransport}$, such that $\Xi$ equals $\eta$ applied to $t$ over the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, up to a power of $r$, to acting by $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$) and `heqW` (an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds, up to a power of $r$, to acting by $g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$). The four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` express that pairs (curve, rigidification) whose leg is normalised to $\psi \circ F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ and whose associated Deligne datum is $P$ exist (`hK1`), are unique up to an isomorphism compatible with the rigidifications (`hK2`), are stable under base change (`hK3`), and lift along surjections with square-zero-like kernels (`hK4`). The clauses `hC0e` and `hC0u` give existence and uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport $\mathrm{IsNormLevelTransport}$ of $P_0$ along a rigidification. A map $\Theta_f$ into the nilpotent points of $f_M$ with `hnat` (naturality), `hG` ($G$-equivariance), `hC2` (its first component is the fine moduli point of the pair consisting of the curve and its transported level-$n$ structure) and `hC2c` (composing with $p$ gives the coarse moduli point of the curve). A homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$ and the clause `hC3`, which for a normalised pair $(E,\varrho)$ with datum $P$ and for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ produces a further rigidification $\varrho'$ whose datum is the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twist $P'$ of $P$, whose level-$n$ transport differs from that of $\varrho$ by the twist $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and for which extra level structures at any prime $\ell \neq r$ invertible in the base, transported from an $e\gamma$-stable extra level of $A_0$ along $\varrho$ and along $\varrho'$, have the same points.
--
--   **The specific situation.** An algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to k$, Deligne data $P, P'$ over $k$, fake elliptic curves $E, E'$ over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho$ of $E$ and $\varrho'$ of $E'$ relative to $A_0$ and the normalised leg $\psi \circ F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$, the hypotheses `hΞψ`, `hev`, `hΞψ'`, `hev'` that $\Xi$ of each pair has the normalised leg and that the associated Deligne datum, transported by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, is $P$ respectively $P'$; an isomorphism $i : E.A \cong E'.A$ over $k$ with $\mathrm{IsoVia}$ (compatibility with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-actions and the level-$N$ structures). Further, $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$, a third rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E$ with `hev''` (normalised leg and associated datum $P'$), the hypothesis `htw` that the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$, the hypothesis `htr` that $\varrho''$ is the $e\gamma$-translate of $\varrho$ in the sense of $\mathrm{IsTranslateBy}$, and the hypothesis `hcorr` that $\varrho''$ and $\varrho'$ are matched through $i$: there are maps $i_b$ on the reductions and $u_A$ on the $A_0$-parts, compatible with $g_b$, the structure morphisms and $g_A$, with $u_A$ a pullback along the identity, and natural numbers $i_1, j_1$ such that $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, $u_A$ and multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \neq r$ such that $\ell$ is a unit in $k$, for every extra level structure at $\ell$ on $A_0$ (the bound variable for it reuses the name `K₀`, shadowing the fraction field) and for all extra level structures $C$ and $C''$ at $\ell$ on $E$ — an extra level structure consisting of a closed immersion into the curve which is a finite flat $\Lambda$-stable subgroup of $\ell$-torsion of rank $\ell^{2}$, disjoint from the level-$N$ structure and geometrically isomorphic to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{2}$ — the following holds. Assume:
--
--   (i) $C$ is transported into the base extra level along $\varrho$: for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t'$ from $T$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ and every point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$, if $R$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$ factors through the closed immersion of $C$, then $R$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ and then by $\varrho.g_A$ factors through the closed immersion of the base extra level;
--
--   (ii) the same condition for $C''$ with $\varrho''$ in place of $\varrho$;
--
--   (iii) $C$ and $C''$ have the same points over $k$: for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t$ from $T$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ and every point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, $R$ factors through the closed immersion of $C$ if and only if it factors through that of $C''$.
--
--   Then the base extra level is stable under $e\gamma$ on points whose base factors through $\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ along the residue leg: for every scheme $T$ and every pair of morphisms $t$ from $T$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi))$ and $t'$ from $T$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ such that $t'$ followed by the morphism induced by $\mathrm{residueLeg}\,\pi$ of the normalised leg $\psi \circ F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ equals $t$, and for every point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$, if $R$ factors through the closed immersion of the base extra level then so does $R$ followed by $e\gamma$.
--
--   This is the detection step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for the $r$-adic uniformisation of the quaternionic (Shimura) curve: equality of the two extra level structures at $\ell$ obtained by transporting one and the same base extra level along a rigidification and along its $e_\gamma$-translate forces that base level to be stable under $e_\gamma$, over bases lying over the residue field of $k$. It is the converse direction to the last clause of the translation hypothesis `hC3`, and it feeds the corresponding statement in which the stability is asserted over all bases over $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$.
